{"name":"Abduction","hex":"#166461","fetched":"2026-10-19","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"abduction","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A leading away; a carrying away. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The act of abducing or abducting; a drawing apart; the movement which separates a limb or other part from the axis, or middle line, of the body."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abduction"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kidnapping","blocks":[{"text":"Kidnapping is the illegal relocation (abduction) and confinement of a person against their will, and is a crime in many jurisdictions. Kidnapping may be accomplished by use of force or fear, or a victim may be enticed into confinement by fraud or deception. Kidnapping is distinguished from false imprisonment by the intentional movement of the victim to a different location."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Dinah_tissot.jpg/330px-Dinah_tissot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kidnapping","wikidata":"Q318296"},{"title":"Alien abduction","blocks":[{"text":"Alien abduction is the phenomenon claimed by people reporting that they or their patients have been kidnapped by extraterrestrial beings and subjected to physical and/or psychological experimentation. Most scientists and mental health professionals explain these experiences by factors such as suggestibility, sleep paralysis, deception, and psychopathology. Skeptic Robert Sheaffer sees similarity between some of the aliens described by abductees and those depicted in science fiction films, in particular Invaders From Mars (1953)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Walton%28reconstitution%29.png/330px-Walton%28reconstitution%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alien_abduction","wikidata":"Q892757"},{"title":"Abduction (2011 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Abduction is a 2011 American action thriller film directed by John Singleton, produced by Roy Lee and Ellen Goldsmith-Vein, and written by Shawn Christensen. The film stars Taylor Lautner in the lead role, alongside Lily Collins, Alfred Molina, Jason Isaacs, Maria Bello, and Sigourney Weaver in supporting roles. The film follows a young man who sets out to uncover the truth about his life after finding a photo of himself as a child on a missing persons website. The film was released by Lionsgate on September 23, 2011, and grossed $82.1 million on a $35 million budget."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/5b/Abduction_Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abduction_(2011_film)","wikidata":"Q143716"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Dinah_tissot.jpg/500px-Dinah_tissot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Dinah_tissot.jpg/500px-Dinah_tissot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The abduction of Dinah (watercolor, c. 1896–1902 by James Tissot)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADinah_tissot.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/March_2017-_Coors_Kidnapping_Ransom_Note_%2833460504411%29.jpg/500px-March_2017-_Coors_Kidnapping_Ransom_Note_%2833460504411%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/March_2017-_Coors_Kidnapping_Ransom_Note_%2833460504411%29.jpg/500px-March_2017-_Coors_Kidnapping_Ransom_Note_%2833460504411%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMarch_2017-_Coors_Kidnapping_Ransom_Note_(3346050441